1e:["$","div",null,{"className":"bg-amber-50 border-l-4 border-amber-400 rounded-xl p-6 mb-10","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2","children":"What This Coursework Is"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-800 leading-relaxed","children":"IMPORTANT — this is not an EMT course and completing it certifies nothing. EMT certification requires a state-approved program with classroom, skills laboratory, and clinical or field hours, followed by the cognitive and psychomotor examinations your state requires (most states use the NREMT exams) and certification or licensure by your state EMS office. The psychomotor component — airway management, splinting, spinal motion restriction, lifting and moving — is assessed by hands-on demonstration and cannot be delivered or verified online by anyone. Any provider offering online-only EMT certification is not offering a recognized credential. Nothing here is a clinical protocol: real scope of practice is set by your state and your service's medical director, and their protocols govern."}]]}]
